// Declaring the same variable twice in one block is a redefinition, not an assignment. The second
// declaration must be a clear error (previously it was silently dropped while its initializer still
// ran as a write - last-wins with no diagnostic). Sibling for-loop init vars and nested-block
// shadowing are separate scopes and remain legal (covered by the e2e suite).
int32 main() {
    int32 x = 1;
    int32 x = 2;
    return x;
}
